  }))), "Errors and limitations of the LLM"), mdx("p", null, "Here are a few things that felt like clear limitations, though perhaps some of them could be corrected through more careful prompting:\nIt seemed like over the course of the conversation the LLM narrowed in on an increasingly small number of takeaway points that it reiterated over and over again. The survey paper I was working on is 28 pages long with wide-ranging content, including technical descriptions of some of the wide-array of existing approaches to studying LSC. Most of this the LLM did not touch in its various responses, and even though some of the points it zeroed in on are also of interest to me (as noted above), I had been hoping it would give me more novel insight into other parts of the paper.\nIts natural response style seemed unnecessarily longwinded. Although it often provided helpful tables and single sentence summaries, it ultimately produced an absolutely enormous amount of text, perhaps even similar to the length of the paper itself. This might be justifiable if it was giving insightful breakdowns of dense parts of the paper, but given the point above, it feels like a genuine limitation."));
